<mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em; margin-left: 0.056em;\"><mjx-TeXAtom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2217\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msubsup space=\"4\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3A6\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.309em; margin-left: 0;\"><mjx-TeXAtom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-TeXAtom><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 0.18em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D449 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2218\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msup space=\"3\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D447 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em; margin-left: 0.056em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-var\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2032\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2218\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msub space=\"3\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3A6\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>∘</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">′</mo></msup><mo>∘</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, and explain in one sentence why this says\nthat the adjoint carries no information the dual map does not, beyond\nthe choice of inner product.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n<p><em>Hint: for (a), both sides send a vector of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"W\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> to a functional on <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"V\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D449 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, so evaluate them at an arbitrary\nvector of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"V\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D449 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</em></p>","file":"ch10-inner-products/06-adjoints.html"}